 \"sha256\": hashlib.sha256(open(self.entry(n), \"rb\").read()).hexdigest()}\nResourceWarning: Enable tracemalloc to get the object allocation traceback\nok\ntest_wrong_data_exits_1_not_3 (test_record.Ledger.test_wrong_data_exits_1_not_3) ... /workspace/record/test_record.py:173: ResourceWarning: unclosed file <_io.BufferedReader name='/tmp/tmpxv6ri8gr/entries/000001.json'>\n  raw = open(self.entry(1), \"rb\").read().replace(b'\"claim\":\"mlp beats linear\"', b'\"claim\":\"\\\\ud800\"')\nResourceWarning: Enable tracemalloc to get the object allocation traceback\n/workspace/record/test_record.py:174: ResourceWarning: unclosed file <_io.BufferedWriter name='/tmp/tmpxv6ri8gr/entries/000001.json'>\n  open(self.entry(1), \"wb\").write(raw)\nResourceWarning: Enable tracemalloc to get the object allocation traceback\nok\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\nRan 21 tests in 0.074s\n\nOK (skipped=1)\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"cd /workspace/record && python3 -m unittest test_record -v","time":{"start":1794917516108,"end":1794917516293}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Now I understand the codebase. Let me analyze what needs to be done:\n\n1. The `check-anchors` command in `record.py` needs a new `--max-pending-hours H` option\n2. When this option is provided, if any range head's proof is still pending (i.e., `check_ots` returns `None`) and its Sigstore attestation time is more than H hours ago, exit 1 with a message containing `still pending N h`\n3. Without the option, behavior is unchanged (pending proofs are accepted)\n4. All existing tests must still pass\n\nLooking at the `cmd_check_anchors` function:\n- It processes anchors and checks both sigstore and ots proofs\n- For ots proofs, `check_ots` returns the earliest Bitcoin block time or `None` if pending\n- The sigstore attestation has an `integrated_time` (returned as `t` from `check_sigstore`)\n\nI need to:\n1. Add the `--max-pending-hours` argument to the `check-anchors` subparser\n2. In `cmd_check_anchors`, track the sigstore attestation time for each range head\n3. When checking ots proofs, if the proof is pending (returns `None`) and `--max-pending-hours` is set, check if the attestation time is more than H hours ago\n4. If so, add to `bad` list with the appropriate message\n\nLet me look at the data flow more carefully:\n- `check_sigstore` returns `(t, pred, commit)` where `t` is the integrated time\n- `check_ots` returns the earliest Bitcoin block time or `None` if pending\n- The `rows` list contains info about each anchor\n- `ranges` contains `(from_seq, to_seq, commit)` for each sigstore anchor\n- `stamped` contains the seq numbers that have ots proofs\n\nI need to track the attestation time for each range head (the `to_seq` in ranges). When we process an ots proof for a range head, we need to know the sigstore attestation time for that same range head.\n\nLet me modify the code to:\n1. Store the attestation time for each range head when processing sigstore anchors\n2. When processing ots anchors, if the proof is pending and `--max-pending-hours` is set, check the attestation time\n\nActually, looking more carefully, the sigstore anchor and ots anchor for the same sequence number are separate files. The sigstore anchor attests to a range ending at `seq`, and the ots anchor is for that same `seq` (the range head).\n\nSo I need to:\n1. When processing sigstore anchors, store the attestation time (`t`) for each `seq` (the range head)\n2. When processing ots anchors for a range head (seq in `stamped`), if `check_ots` returns `None` (pending) and `--max-pending-hours` is set, check if the attestation time for that seq is more than H hours ago\n\nLet me implement this.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_1e96bc348001YPydnc6s7ltV4H","sessionID":"ses_e16947aa2ffe1bQjYy6NyBOia0","messageID":"msg_1e96b93a7001GB65570lBSjfs8"}}
